course: dictionary
lesson: 4638
title: Hints and clues
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A hint is a small clue or piece of help. It shows you the way to an answer without giving the full answer away. «Hint: start by finding the total.» That is a nudge in the right direction, not the answer itself.
explain: A hint can also be a very small amount of something. «A hint of lemon» in a cake means you can just taste a little lemon, not a lot.
explain: To hint is to say something in an indirect way, not plainly. Writers drop small hints to tell readers a secret slowly. «Starting in the middle of the action means the reader is hooked first and learns the background later through small hints.»
fact: A hint is a small clue or piece of help that does not give the full answer.
fact: A hint of something is a very small amount of it, like a hint of lemon.
fact: To hint means to say something indirectly, not plainly.
fact: A clue is a detail in a text that hints at something.
exercise: «Hint: start by finding the total.» What is a hint here? | The final answer, written out for you | A long story about a total | *A small clue that helps you without giving the full answer | A loud shout
exercise: In «a hint of lemon», what does hint mean? | A loud shout | A big bowl of lemons | *A very small amount | A plain warning
exercise: Mum hinted that we were going to the beach. What does hinted mean? | *Said something indirectly, not plainly | Forgot the plan | Shouted the whole plan out loud | Wrote the plan down in full
test: Dad says «I think a surprise is coming», and you guess he is hinting. What is hinting here? | Buying a present | Telling you something plainly | *Saying something in an indirect way, not plainly | Forgetting the surprise
test: In «a hint of salt», what is a hint? | A loud warning | *A very small amount | Half a cup | A recipe book
exam: A clue in a story «hints at something». What does hints at mean? | Makes the story longer | Hides the story from the reader | *Gives a small, indirect sign of | Says the whole secret out loud
